26-49119（Gradio）","zh-Hant":"已知漏洞：CVE-2026-49119（Gradio）","ko":"알려진 취약점: CVE-2026-49119 (Gradio)","de":"Bekannte Schwachstelle: CVE-2026-49119 (Gradio)","fr":"Vulnérabilité connue : CVE-2026-49119 (Gradio)","es":"Vulnerabilidad conocida: CVE-2026-49119 (Gradio)","it":"Vulnerabilità nota: CVE-2026-49119 (Gradio)","pt-PT":"Vulnerabilidade conhecida: CVE-2026-49119 (Gradio)"},"description":{"ja":"NVDの説明（英語原文）: Gradio before 6.16.0 contain a path traversal vulnerability in the FileExplorer component's preprocess() method that allows unauthenticated attackers to escape the configured root directory by supplying path segments containing directory traversal sequences or absolute paths. Attackers can provide crafted path segments that cause os.path.join to discard the root_dir prefix entirely, resulting in arbitrary file read or exposure of sensitive files outside the intended directory.","en":"Gradio before 6.16.0 contain a path traversal vulnerability in the FileExplorer component's preprocess() method that allows unauthenticated attackers to escape the configured root directory by supplying path segments containing directory traversal sequences or absolute paths. Attackers can provide crafted path segments that cause os.path.join to discard the root_dir prefix entirely, resulting in arbitrary file read or exposure of sensitive files outside the intended directory.","zh-Hans":"NVD 说明（英文原文）：Gradio before 6.16.0 contain a path traversal vulnerability in the FileExplorer component's preprocess() method that allows unauthenticated attackers to escape the configured root directory by supplying path segments containing directory traversal sequences or absolute paths. Attackers can provide crafted path segments that cause os.path.join to discard the root_dir prefix entirely, resulting in arbitrary file read or exposure of sensitive files outside the intended directory.","zh-Hant":"NVD 說明（英文原文）：Gradio before 6.16.0 contain a path traversal vulnerability in the FileExplorer compon