 path traversal vulnerability exists in jupyter-server version 2.17.0 due to an incorrect root directory boundary check in the _get_os_path() function within jupyter_server/services/contents/fileio.py. The check uses startswith(root) without appending a trailing path separator, allowing sibling directories with names starting with the same prefix as root_dir to bypass the check. Additionally, the to_os_path() function in utils.py does not strip \"..\" from path parts, enabling traversal sequences","zh-Hant":"NVD 說明（英文原文）：A path traversal vulnerability exists in jupyter-server version 2.17.0 due to an incorrect root directory boundary check in the _get_os_path() function within jupyter_server/services/contents/fileio.py. The check uses startswith(root) without appending a trailing path separator, allowing sibling directories with names starting with the same prefix as root_dir to bypass the check. Additionally, the to_os_path() function in utils.py does not strip \"..\" from path parts, enabling traversal sequences","ko":"NVD 설명(영어 원문): A path traversal vulnerability exists in jupyter-server version 2.17.0 due to an incorrect root directory boundary check in the _get_os_path() function within jupyter_server/services/contents/fileio.py. The check uses startswith(root) without appending a trailing path separator, allowing sibling directories with names starting with the same prefix as root_dir to bypass the check. Additionally, the to_os_path() function in utils.py does not strip \"..\" from path parts, enabling traversal sequences","de":"NVD-Beschreibung (englischer Originaltext): A path traversal vulnerability exists in jupyter-server version 2.17.0 due to an incorrect root directory boundary check in the _get_os_path() function within jupyter_server/services/contents/fileio.py. The check uses startswith(root) without appending a trailing path separator, allowing sibling directories with names starting with the same prefix as root_dir to bypass the check. Additionally, the to_os_path() function in utils.py does not strip \"..\" from path parts, enabling traversal sequences","fr":"Description NVD (texte original en anglais) : A path traversal vulnerability exists in jupyter-server version 2.17.0 due to an incorrect root directory boundary check in the _get_os_path() function within jupyter_server/services/contents/fileio.py. The check uses startswith(root) without appending a trailing path separator, allowing sibling directories with names starting with the same prefix as root_dir to bypass the check. Additionally, the to_os_path() function in utils.py does not strip \"..\" from path parts, enabling traversal sequences","es":"Descripción de NVD (texto original en inglés): A path traversal vulnerability exists in jupyter-server version 2.17.0 due to an incorrect root directory boundary check in the _get_os_path() function within jupyter_server/services/contents/fileio.py. The check uses startswith(root) without appending a trailing path separator, allowing sibling directories with names starting with the same prefix as root_dir to bypass the check. Additionally, the to_os_path() function in utils.py does not strip \"..\" from path parts, enabling traversal sequences","it":"Descrizione NVD (testo originale in inglese): A path traversal vulnerability exists in jupyter-server version 2.17.0 due to an incorrect root directory boundary check in the _get_os_path() function within jupyter_server/services/contents/fileio.py. The check uses startswith(root) without appending a trailing path separator, allowing sibling directories with names starting with the same prefix as root_dir to bypass the check. Additionally, the to_os_path() function in utils.py does not strip \"..\" from path parts, enabling traversal sequences","pt-PT":"Descrição do NVD (texto original em inglês): A path traversal vulnerability exists in jupyter-server version 2.17.0 due to an incorrect root directory boundary check in the _get_os_path() function within jupyter_server/services/contents/fileio.py. The check uses startswith(root) without appending a trailing path separator, allowing sibling directories with names starting with the same prefix as root_dir to bypass the check. Additionally, the to_os_path() function in utils.py does not strip \"..\" from path parts, enabling traversal sequences"},"recommendation":{"ja":"Jupyter Server を CVE-2026-5422 の影響を受けないバージョンへ早急にアップグレードし、それまでは認証なしでのネットワークアクセスを制限してください。","en":"Upgrade Jupyter Server to a version not affected by CVE-2026-5422 as soon as possible, and restrict unauthenticated network access to it in the meantime.","zh-Hans":"请尽快将 Jupyter Server 升级到不受 CVE-2026-5422 影响的版本，在此之前请限制对其的未认证网络访问。","zh-Hant":"請儘快將 Jupyter Server 升級到不受 CVE-2026-5422 影響的版本，在此之前請限制對其的未經驗證網路存取。","ko":"Jupyter Server을(를) CVE-2026-5422의 영향을 받지 않는 버전으로 가능한 한 빨리 업그레이드하고, 그때까지는 인증 없는 네트워크 접근을 제한하세요.","de":"Aktualisieren Sie Jupyter Server so schnell wie möglich auf eine Version, die von CVE-2026-5422 nicht betroffen ist, und beschränken Sie in der Zwischenzeit den unauthentifizierten Netzwerkzugriff darauf.","fr":"Mettez à niveau Jupyter Server dès que possible vers une version non affectée par CVE-2026-5422 et, en attendant, restreignez l'accès réseau non authentifié.","es":"Actualice Jupyter Server lo antes posible a una versión no afectada por CVE-2026-5422 y, mientras tanto, restrinja el acceso de red sin autenticación.","it":"Aggiorna Jupyter Server il prima possibile a una versione non interessata da CVE-2026-5422 e, nel frattempo, limita l'accesso di rete non autenticato.","pt-PT":"Atualize o Jupyter Server o quanto antes para uma versão não afetada por CVE-2026-5422 e, entretanto, restrinja o acesso de rede não autenticado."}},{"cveId":"CVE-2026-6657","signatureId":"jupyter-noauth","minVersion":[1,12,0],"fixedVersion":[2,17,1],"title":{"ja":"既知の脆弱性: CVE-2026-6657 (Jupyter Server)","en":"Known Vulnerability: CVE-2026-6657 (Jupyter Server)","zh-Hans":"已知漏洞：CVE-2026-6657（Jupyter Server）","zh-Hant":"已知漏洞：CVE-2026-6657（Jupyter Server）","ko":"알려진 취약점: CVE-2026-6657 (Jupyter Server)","de":"Bekannte Schwachstelle: CVE-2026-6657 (Jupyter Server)","fr":"Vulnérabilité connue : CVE-2026-6657 (Jupyter Server)","es":"Vulnerabilidad conocida: CVE-2026-6657 (Jupyter Server)","it":"Vulnerabilità nota: CVE-2026-6657 (Jupyter Server)","pt-PT":"Vulnerabilidade conhecida: CVE-2026-6657 (Jupyter Server)"},"description":{"ja":"NVDの説明（英語原文）: A vulnerability in jupyter-server versions 1.12.0 through 2.17.0 allows an attacker to bypass CORS origin validation when the `allow_origin_pat` configuration is used. The issue arises from the use of `re.match()` for validating the `Origin` header, which only anchors at the start of the string. This allows attacker-controlled domains such as `trusted.example.com.evil.com` to pass validation against patterns intended to match `trusted.example.com`. The vulnerability affects multiple locations in","en":"A vulnerability in jupyter-server versions 1.12.0 through 2.17.0 allows an attacker to bypass CORS origin validation when the `allow_origin_pat` configuration is used. The issue arises from the use of `re.match()` for validating the `Origin` header, which only anchors at the start of the string. This allows attacker-controlled domains such as `trusted.example.com.evil.com` to pass validation against patterns intended to match `trusted.example.com`. The vulnerability affects multiple locations in","zh-Hans":"NVD 说明（英文原文）：A vulnerability in jupyter-server versions 1.12.0 through 2.17.0 allows an attacker to bypass CORS origin validation when the `allow_origin_pat` configuration is used. The issue arises from the use of `re.match()` for validating the `Origin` header, which only anchors at the start of the string. This allows attacker-controlled domains such as `trusted.example.com.evil.com` to pass validation against patterns intended to match `trusted.example.com`. The vulnerability affects multiple locations in","zh-Hant":"NVD 說明（英文原文）：A vulnerabilit